-- title:
--   Additivity of the Gauss order on the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e, t$ be natural numbers with $1 \le e$ and $t \le e$. Write $R = W[[X_0,X_1]]$ for the ring of formal power series in two variables over $W$ and let `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)` be the quotient of $R$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \varpi^{e}$, the constant power series of $\varpi^e$ being subtracted. For $x$ in this quotient, `gaussOrder` of $x$, taken with respect to the additive valuation `IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal W` with values in $\mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$, with parameters $\varpi^e$, $e$ and $t$, is defined as the supremum, over all power series $F \in R$ whose class in the quotient is $x$, of the quantity $\inf_{d}\bigl(v(\mathrm{coeff}_d F) + \mathrm{annulusWeight}\,e\,t\,d\bigr)$, the infimum being over all multidegrees $d \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to_{f} \mathbb{N}$ and the weights being given by the function `annulusWeight`. The theorem asserts that for all $x, y$ in the quotient this invariant is additive: the Gauss order of $x \cdot y$ equals the sum of the Gauss orders of $x$ and of $y$, as elements of $\mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$.
--
--   This is the Gauss-lemma statement for the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^{e})$: the depth-$t$ Gauss order, which measures the valuation of the coefficients of a representing power series weighted along the circle of the annulus corresponding to $t$, is multiplicative, so that it behaves like an additive valuation on the model. It is used in the treatment of prolongation tuples and place specialisation, where Gauss orders of products and powers of elements of such models are compared.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_gaussOrder_mul.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_UVCrossingGaussOrder

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open ModularCurve ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel

theorem ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.gaussOrder_mul
    {W : Type u} [CommRing W] [IsDomain W] [IsDiscreteValuationRing W]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal W) W]
    (ϖ : W) (hϖ : Irreducible ϖ) (e t : ℕ) (he : 1 ≤ e) (ht : t ≤ e)
    (x y : UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)) :
    gaussOrder (IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal W) (ϖ ^ e) e t (x * y) =
      gaussOrder (IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal W) (ϖ ^ e) e t x +
        gaussOrder (IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal W) (ϖ ^ e) e t y := by sorry
